Ahead of the announcement of the Apple Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4 later this week, code in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/watchos-27/">watchOS 27</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> betas points to a series of new features for the product line.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/apple-watch-series-12.png" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1060718" /><br/>
The information comes from a <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/watchos-27-hints-at-new-readiness-app-improved-strength-workout-metrics-models-with-new-optical-sensor-family-and-128gb-of-storage.2488563/">new post</a> from <em>MacRumors</em> forums member "pdfu." The findings include:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>New "Readiness" app</strong>: An all-new separate Watch app referred to in code as "Readiness," distinct from the existing Vitals app. The &zwnj;watchOS 27&zwnj; launcher apparently includes it in the default <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/home-screen/">Home Screen</a> layout immediately after the Workout app, and the Watch companion app on &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; references the same app in its logic for arranging apps on the &zwnj;Home Screen&zwnj;. Its name and placement next to the Workout app suggest Apple is preparing a more substantial readiness or recovery experience for the Apple Watch.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Richer strength workouts</strong>: Expanded health infrastructure to store individual sets, repetition counts, weight, equipment, body side, and duration.</li><br/>
<li><strong>New optical-sensing system</strong>: A new sensor family called "Sunstone4p0" with lower noise coefficients, and wrist- and orientation-based channel selection. This could point to revised heart-sensing hardware on an upcoming Apple Watch, featuring improved readings when the reflected pulse signal is weak and specialized sensing according to the watch's placement.</li><br/>
<li><strong>128GB storage</strong>: A NAND storage profile tied to the T8320 chip for the Apple Watch Series 12 and Apple Watch Ultra 4 suggesting that they could offer 128GB of storage, up from 64GB on previous models.</li> </ul><br/>
<br/>
<em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-watch-series-12-to-get-fitness-upgrades/">previously reported</a> that the Apple Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4 will tout new health and fitness features.<br/>
<br/>
pdfu has emerged as an intriguing source of code discoveries in recent weeks. The forum member previously spotted references to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/04/macos-26-7-code-game-controllers/">two unreleased game controllers</a> in the first macOS 26.7 release candidate, identified by the internal names T6502 and T1057, and separately found evidence in audioOS 27 beta 8 pointing to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/04/apple-testing-four-homepod-surround-system/">a four-speaker HomePod surround sound system</a> and a new "Party Mode" feature.<br/>
